```rust
pub fn resolve(&self, roots: &AnchorRoots, containment: Containment) -> Result<PathBuf, AnchorError> {
    let root = self
        .anchor
        .root(roots)
        .ok_or(AnchorError::AnchorRootAbsent { anchor: self.anchor })?;

    // Layer 1 (always, even for absent paths): the stored remainder is
    // untrusted at read time. Reject every component that is not
    // `Normal` — `ParentDir`/`RootDir`/`Prefix`/`CurDir` — so a tampered
    // `..`, leading `/`, `.`, or drive prefix can never escape the root.
    // Also reject an empty remainder (the root itself) — rooting at the
    // anchor itself is dangerous.
    let relative = Path::new(&self.relative);
    let is_traversal =
        self.relative.is_empty() || !relative.components().all(|c| matches!(c, Component::Normal(_)));
    if is_traversal {
        return Err(AnchorError::TraversalAttempt {
            relative: self.relative.clone(),
        });
    }

    let candidate = root.join(relative);

    // Layer 2 catches a symlink routing a Normal-only path outside the root. `exists()` is false for
    // a dangling symlink, so the symlink test is required, or the guard is skipped and the join
    // returned unvalidated (a dangling symlink instead fails canonicalize with a safe `Io` error).
    // `dunce::canonicalize` is required, or Windows `\\?\` UNC paths give false negatives.
    // Containment compares whole components (`Path::starts_with`); a string-prefix check accepts a
    // sibling like `<root>-evil`. The canonical path is returned so callers act on what was validated.
    // The leaf is stat'ed once, before canonicalize, for both the branch and the carve-out below; a
    // later stat (`Path::is_symlink()` is one) widens the TOCTOU window in the exploitable direction.
    let leaf_is_symlink = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&candidate).is_ok_and(|m| m.file_type().is_symlink());
    if !candidate.exists() && !leaf_is_symlink {
        return Ok(candidate);
    }

    let canon_root = dunce::canonicalize(&root).map_err(|source| AnchorError::Io {
        path: root.clone(),
        source,
    })?;
    let canon_candidate = dunce::canonicalize(&candidate).map_err(|source| AnchorError::Io {
        path: candidate.clone(),
        source,
    })?;

    // Return the canonicalized path (not the raw join) to close the
    // TOCTOU window: the caller acts on the symlink-resolved path that
    // was verified to be within the anchor root.
    if canon_candidate.starts_with(&canon_root) {
        return Ok(canon_candidate);
    }

    // Exhaustive match, never `==`: a future third variant must be
    // classified here or the build breaks — the fail-closed
    // discipline the `Containment` doc claims.
    match containment {
        // Unix only: the layouts this exists for (GNU stow, yadm,
        // an iCloud/Dropbox-synced config dir) are Unix-only, and
        // `is_symlink()` does not cover every Windows reparse tag
        // (`LX_SYMLINK`, `APPEXECLINK`, WCI) — a security guard
        // must not rest on that predicate. On Windows the variant
        // is a synonym for `Strict`.
        #[cfg(unix)]
        Containment::AllowRelocatedAncestor if !leaf_is_symlink => {
            // `warn!`, not `debug!`: every destructive caller
            // refuses this path, so this is the only signal that
            // grim is reading through a relocated ancestor.
            tracing::warn!(
                anchor = %self.anchor,
                path = %canon_candidate.display(),
                "resolving through a relocated ancestor outside the anchor root"
            );
            Ok(canon_candidate)
        }
        Containment::AllowRelocatedFile => {
            tracing::debug!(
                anchor = %self.anchor,
                path = %canon_candidate.display(),
                "resolving a relocated config file outside the anchor root"
            );
            Ok(canon_candidate)
        }
        Containment::AllowRelocatedAncestor | Containment::Strict => Err(AnchorError::EscapedAnchor {
            anchor: self.anchor,
            resolved: canon_candidate,
        }),
    }
}
```

- Layer-1 component loop replaced with a single `is_traversal` bool (`.all()` + `is_empty()`), one error return instead of a `for` loop with an inline early return.
- Inverted the Layer-2 existence check to an early return (`!exists && !symlink → Ok(candidate)`), removing one level of nesting for the rest of the function.
- Split root/candidate canonicalization and the containment check out of the old `if candidate.exists() || leaf_is_symlink { … }` block now that the non-existent case returns early.
- Turned the trailing `Containment::AllowRelocatedAncestor | Containment::Strict => {}` no-op arm plus the shared `return Err(EscapedAnchor)` after the match into a single arm that returns the error directly — same three outcomes, no fallthrough.

```rust
pub fn resolve(&self, roots: &AnchorRoots, containment: Containment) -> Result<PathBuf, AnchorError> {
    let root = self
        .anchor
        .root(roots)
        .ok_or(AnchorError::AnchorRootAbsent { anchor: self.anchor })?;

    // Layer 1: reject an empty remainder or any non-`Normal` component
    // (`..`, leading `/`, `.`, drive prefix) before touching the filesystem.
    let relative = Path::new(&self.relative);
    let is_traversal = self.relative.is_empty()
        || relative.components().any(|c| !matches!(c, Component::Normal(_)));
    if is_traversal {
        return Err(AnchorError::TraversalAttempt {
            relative: self.relative.clone(),
        });
    }

    let candidate = root.join(relative);

    // Layer 2: only needed once something exists at `candidate` (a dangling
    // symlink included) — an absent, non-symlink candidate can't have been
    // routed outside the root, so it is returned unvalidated below.
    let leaf_is_symlink = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&candidate).is_ok_and(|m| m.file_type().is_symlink());
    if !candidate.exists() && !leaf_is_symlink {
        return Ok(candidate);
    }

    let canon_root = dunce::canonicalize(&root).map_err(|source| AnchorError::Io {
        path: root.clone(),
        source,
    })?;
    let canon_candidate = dunce::canonicalize(&candidate).map_err(|source| AnchorError::Io {
        path: candidate.clone(),
        source,
    })?;

    // Contained: return the canonicalized path, not the raw join, so the
    // caller acts on what was actually verified.
    if canon_candidate.starts_with(&canon_root) {
        return Ok(canon_candidate);
    }

    // Escaped the root — exhaustive match, never `==`, so a future variant
    // must be classified here or the build breaks.
    match containment {
        #[cfg(unix)]
        Containment::AllowRelocatedAncestor if !leaf_is_symlink => {
            tracing::warn!(
                anchor = %self.anchor,
                path = %canon_candidate.display(),
                "resolving through a relocated ancestor outside the anchor root"
            );
            Ok(canon_candidate)
        }
        Containment::AllowRelocatedFile => {
            tracing::debug!(
                anchor = %self.anchor,
                path = %canon_candidate.display(),
                "resolving a relocated config file outside the anchor root"
            );
            Ok(canon_candidate)
        }
        Containment::AllowRelocatedAncestor | Containment::Strict => Err(AnchorError::EscapedAnchor {
            anchor: self.anchor,
            resolved: canon_candidate,
        }),
    }
}
```

